## How to use this checklist

For each Tier 1/2 component from `handoff/components-priority.md`:

1. Read the **Source scoring** (`extract/components.md`).
2. Read the **License verdict** (`extract/license-audit.md`) — if
   incompatible, the choice collapses to either `wrap/adapter`
   (incompatible but compatible surface) or `don't port`.
3. Mark one option with `[x]`. Justify in one line citing the
   C1-C6 scores.
4. Note the **Effort estimate** for the chosen option. Effort is
   P (≤ 1 day), M (≤ 1 week), G (≥ 1 week).

A component you mark `don't port` is still worth understanding — keep
the entry; the *why* matters as much as the *what*.

