## Decision vocabulary

`reuse direct` — copy the component as-is into your downstream.
Only valid when license permits redistribution *and* your
deployment model is compatible (e.g. LGPL requires dynamic
linking).

`wrap/adapter` — keep the component as an external dependency;
write a thin adapter in your codebase to translate its surface to
your idioms. Use when license is permissive but the upstream API
doesn't match yours.

`clean-room` — re-implement following
`handoff/implementation-guide.md`. Use when:
- License is incompatible with your licensing model.
- The component is tightly coupled to its original platform.
- You want to evolve it independently of upstream.

`don't port` — explicitly skip. Use when:
- The component solves a problem your downstream doesn't have.
- A standard library or third-party package covers the same need.
- Score < 30 and not worth even a wrapper.

